proof_plan:
Each Boolean axiom, such as $\eqclass {\phi \land \paren {\psi \lor \chi} } {} = \eqclass {\paren {\phi \land \psi} \lor \paren {\phi \land \chi} } {}$, holds because the corresponding biconditional is a [[Definition:Tautology|tautology]], hence a theorem of $T$.
As $T$ is consistent, $\eqclass \top {} \ne \eqclass \bot {}$.
{{qed}}
